Below is a step-by-step recipe you can copy-paste into a MapLibre GL JS app to turn a **raster-DEM** tile set into a hillshade layer.

---

## 1. Add the DEM source to the style

```js
// Inside map.on('load', …) or before you call map.addLayer()
map.addSource('my-dem', {
  type: 'raster-dem',          // <-- tells MapLibre this is elevation data
  url: 'https://example.com/tiles/{z}/{x}/{y}.png', // any raster-DEM tile URL
  // optional but recommended:
  tileSize: 256,               // 256 px (or 512 if your tiles are that size)
  maxzoom: 14,                 // highest zoom you have tiles for
  // If your DEM tiles are encoded as 16-bit PNG/TIFF you can add:
  // encoding: 'mapbox'   // for Mapbox-style elevation encoding
});
```

* **`type: 'raster-dem'`** is the only source type that hillshade can read.  
* The URL can be a TileJSON endpoint (`url: 'https://myserver.com/dem.json'`) or a simple XYZ template as shown.  
* Make sure the server sends the correct CORS headers (`Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *` or your domain) so the browser can fetch the tiles.

---

## 2. Add the hillshade layer

```js
map.addLayer({
  id: 'hillshade',
  type: 'hillshade',
  source: 'my-dem',            // matches the source name above
  // optional: limit the layer to a specific zoom range
  minzoom: 0,
  maxzoom: 14,

  // Paint properties – tweak to get the look you want
  paint: {
    // Light direction (azimuth, in degrees clockwise from north)
    'hillshade-illumination-direction': 315,

    // How strong the shading looks (default 0.5)
    'hillshade-exaggeration': 0.5,

    // Colors – you can keep the defaults or customize
    'hillshade-shadow-color': 'rgba(0,0,0,0.5)',
    'hillshade-highlight-color': 'rgba(255,255,255,0.5)',
    'hillshade-accent-color': 'rgba(255,255,255,0.2)'
  }
});
```

### What the paint properties do

| Property | Meaning | Typical range |
|----------|---------|---------------|
| `hillshade-illumination-direction` | Sun azimuth (0 = north, 90 = east) | 0-360 |
| `hillshade-exaggeration` | Boosts the apparent relief | 0-1 (or higher for dramatic effect) |
| `hillshade-shadow-color` | Color of the “shadowed” side | any CSS color |
| `hillshade-highlight-color` | Color of the illuminated side | any CSS color |
| `hillshade-accent-color` | Color for the “mid-tone” slope | any CSS color |

---

## 3. (Optional) Add a terrain source for 3-D extrusion

If you also want to enable true 3-D terrain (e.g. drape other layers over the DEM), add a **terrain** source:

```js
map.setTerrain({
  source: 'my-dem',
  exaggeration: 1.5   // make mountains look taller
});
```

> **Note:** The hillshade layer works **without** a terrain source; the terrain call is only needed for 3-D visualisation.

---

## 4. Full minimal example

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8" />
  <title>MapLibre Hillshade Demo</title>
  <script src="https://unpkg.com/maplibre-gl@latest/dist/maplibre-gl.js"></script>
  <link href="https://unpkg.com/maplibre-gl@latest/dist/maplibre-gl.css" rel="stylesheet" />
  <style>
    #map { position:absolute; top:0; bottom:0; width:100%; }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
<div id="map"></div>
<script>
  const map = new maplibregl.Map({
    container: 'map',
    style: 'https://demotiles.maplibre.org/style.json', // any base style
    center: [-122.447303, 37.753574],
    zoom: 12,
    // CJK/ideograph handling is irrelevant here, but you can set it if you need it
    // localIdeographFontFamily: 'sans-serif'
  });

  map.on('load', () => {
    // 1️⃣ DEM source
    map.addSource('my-dem', {
      type: 'raster-dem',
      url: 'https://example.com/dem/{z}/{x}/{y}.png',
      tileSize: 256,
      maxzoom: 14
    });

    // 2️⃣ Hillshade layer
    map.addLayer({
      id: 'hillshade',
      type: 'hillshade',
      source: 'my-dem',
      paint: {
        'hillshade-illumination-direction': 315,
        'hillshade-exaggeration': 0.6,
        'hillshade-shadow-color': 'rgba(0,0,0,0.5)',
        'hillshade-highlight-color': 'rgba(255,255,255,0.5)'
      }
    });

    // 3️⃣ (optional) 3-D terrain
    // map.setTerrain({ source: 'my-dem', exaggeration: 1.5 });
  });
</script>
</body>
</html>
```

---

## 5. Common pitfalls & troubleshooting

| Symptom | Likely cause | Fix |
|---------|--------------|-----|
| **No hillshade appears** | DEM source not loading (404, CORS) | Open the tile URL in the browser; check network tab for CORS errors. |
| **Only a flat gray surface** | `raster-dem` tiles are not encoded as elevation (e.g., plain imagery) | Use true elevation tiles (16-bit PNG/TIFF, or Mapbox-style encoding). |
| **Hillshade looks too flat** | `hillshade-exaggeration` is low (default 0.5) | Increase the value (e.g., `0.8` or `1.0`). |
| **Colors look wrong** | Paint colors overridden by a later style layer | Ensure the hillshade layer is added **after** any background/symbol layers you want it to sit beneath, or set its `layout: { visibility: 'visible' }` explicitly. |
| **Performance drops at high zoom** | Very high-resolution DEM tiles (512 px) with many requests | Use a lower `maxzoom` for the DEM source or serve a lower-resolution tile set for zooms > 12. |

---

